## 6. Validation batches

Cite relevant existing test paths/check IDs in this section or the AC mapping. Mark coverage as reuse/extend/new,
and name the uncovered behavior for new cases. Extend existing fixtures first; justify similar tests at distinct
boundaries. Do not duplicate suites or add Goal-specific checks solely to produce fresh evidence. This is not a
new inventory or permission to omit required regression/local/hosted/security checks.

Before every batch: fetch and assess target-delta relevance to validation and authority. Reconcile relevant/unknown
changes; record any permitted irrelevant-delta deferral under the validation policy. Reconcile before final/MR and run
{{PRE_BATCH_ENV_CHECK}}. Batches finish, fix, rerun, advance. Manual feedback precedes final qualification.

| Batch | Runs | Evidence |
|---|---|---|

Give executable selectors, dependency order, safe parallel batches and resource reservations/serial builds.
Estimate implementation effort separately from elapsed build/test time and review/queue waits, citing known
timings or labeling estimates/unknowns. Use existing evidence; no extra timing campaign or separate report.

## 7. Delegation

Carry forward the Goal/Spec priority, normally high when unspecified. Target 3–5
parallel implementation workers for high priority or 1–3 for low whenever useful
independent work, exclusive write ownership, native/resource capacity and budget
permit. These are concurrent implementation workers in dependency-ready phases,
excluding planner/coordinator/reviewers. State concrete constraints when fewer
workers are feasible. The planner may remain a single agent. Low-priority work
may use one worker within its target and yield capacity to the main implementation.

| Phase / ready condition | Worker role / count | Exclusive writable paths | Bound inputs / dependencies | Integration owner / resource reservation |
|---|---|---|---|---|

Use worker names `<task-id>-agent-<id>-<role>` where supported. At implementation
kickoff, verify readiness and dispatch the accepted allocation/sequence; record
actual allocation changes and their reasons in the Result, applying normal review
to material changes. Dispatch later workers as their planned dependencies close.
Reclaim finished workers at handback. See
[parallel scheduling](../../../.agents/skills/restruct-sdlc/sdlc-management/references/coordination.md#default-to-safe-parallel-work-lanes).

